          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નિરાકરણ — nirākaraṇ — \"a solution (to a problem); a settling\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "જો બંને બાજુ વાત કરશે તો આ વિવાદનું નિરાકરણ થશે. jo banne bāju vāt karśe to ā vivādnũ nirākaraṇ thaśe. If both sides talk, this dispute will be settled."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "નિરાકરણ (nirākaraṇ) is a tatsama, borrowed from Sanskrit nirākaraṇa, \"driving away, removing\" (Monier-Williams). Gujarati uses it for clearing a problem away: its solution, a sense the source does not give."
            }
          ]
        },
